From: Pixelado Dev <350114043+pixeladodev@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Menu: what Pixelado Party's menu needs from BananaDS's menu

The in-game menu stays BananaDS's own (src/menu.c): Pixelado Party draws its own menu when it runs
the engine (0008), and menu.c is what opens without Party. This adds to menu.c what Party's menu
needs from the engine:

- bmenu_ext_open / _set / _tick / _close / _sound (menu.h): the volume, the brightness and the FPS
  counter set as menu.c sets them (BananaLinux's volume script, both backlights by the same step,
  "<top> <bottom>" in /data/banana/backlight at close), the handheld's own keys read back twice a
  second, and the menu's sounds (loaded on their own, without the menu's panels).
- The game's name: looked up again when the game changes (in a Party room the frontend names the
  game chosen, Emu::rom_path, not the room's own program from the command line); a file name that
  says nothing ("4785", "rom") gives way to the cartridge banner's title; the DS menu is "DS menu".
- A backlight that can't be written is logged once.
- Fonts: BananaOS's Inter before DejaVu Sans when Pixelify Sans is missing, so the menu always opens.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
